From 2678da0c9354dbee74987b6b851477b3127932ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 17:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add energy-model-core v1 with replay engine, sensor geometry,
 validation and unit tests

### Motivation

- Introduce a deterministic two-node energy model core to compute stored/usable/immediate energy from tank readings and geometry.
- Enable replaying historical readings across sensor-geometry epochs and tank DNA calibration windows to support model validation and event detection.
- Provide a validation pipeline that produces metrics, events, visualization data and CSV export to help evaluate model accuracy.

### Description

- Add `lib/energyModelV2/energyModelCore.ts` implementing tank observation conversion, two-node energy calculations, Newton cooling, fixed heating distribution, state advance logic and a `runEnergyModelCoreReplay` wrapper.
- Add `lib/energyModelV2/replayEngine.ts` to normalize and order readings, resolve sensor geometry per timestamp, select tank DNA profiles, and drive a generic replay stepper.
- Add `lib/energyModelV2/sensorGeometry.ts` and `lib/energyModelV2/tankDna.ts` for sensor epoch handling and tank DNA profile utilities.
- Add `lib/energyModelV2/replayValidation.ts` to create validation steps, detect events, compute metrics (MAE/RMSE/max), export CSV and assemble a validation report and visualization payload.
- Add unit tests for the above modules: `sensorGeometry.test.ts`, `replayEngine.test.ts`, `energyModelCore.test.ts` and `replayValidation.test.ts`.
- Wire the new unit tests into the existing forecast test runner by updating `scripts/run-tank-temperature-forecast-tests.ts` and `tsconfig.forecast-tests.json`.
- Add a new `tsconfig.replay-validation.json`, a CLI script `scripts/runReplayValidation.ts` to fetch readings and persist validation artifacts, and an npm script `replay:validate` in `package.json` for running the replay validation build/runner.

### Testing

- Compiled the new replay validation target with `tsc -p tsconfig.replay-validation.json` as part of the added `replay:validate` flow.
- Executed the forecast test runner which now includes `runSensorGeometryUnitTests`, `runReplayEngineUnitTests`, `runEnergyModelCoreUnitTests` and `runReplayValidationUnitTests`.
- All added unit tests and the integrated test runner steps completed successfully (no failures reported).
